{"content_hash": "6c2cc2b42d575b22", "version_id": 144, "article_id": 15, "level_code": "en_b2", "lang": "en", "level": 4, "level_label": "B2 中高级", "title": "US inmate Christa Pike awake after failed execution", "title_zh": "美国死囚克里斯塔·派克处决失败后苏醒过来", "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c8kgezxn54qko?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/240/cpsprodpb/226c/live/7221efd0-c1c9-11f1-b8a9-47f21beea0a3.jpg", "credit": ""}, "published_date": "2026-10-06", "word_count": 287, "reading_minutes": 1.4, "lead": "Christa Pike, a death row inmate in the US, survived a failed execution last week. Her lawyers say she is now conscious and speaking, which experts describe as unprecedented.", "lead_zh": "美国死囚克里斯塔·派克上周处决失败后幸存。她的律师表示，她现已恢复意识并能说话，专家称这种情况前所未有。", "preview": "Christa Pike, a 50-year-old death row inmate in Tennessee, is conscious and speaking after surviving a failed execution attempt last week, a", "preview_zh": "据律师称，田纳西州50岁死囚克里斯塔·派克上周处决失败后幸存，目前意识清醒并能说话。她仍在医院接受重症监护，并被戴上手铐。派克因1995年谋杀科琳·斯莱默被判处死刑。上周三，她经历两次注射死刑失败后幸存，被送往医院，数天昏迷不醒，医护人员为她清除体内注射的化学物质。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 134, "url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@d7bba21/content/audio/15/en_b2.mp3", "duration": 110.363, "size_bytes": 665856, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 327, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@d7bba21/content/data/versions/144.json", "paragraphs": ["Christa Pike, a 50-year-old death row inmate in Tennessee, is conscious and speaking after surviving a failed execution attempt last week, according to her lawyers. She remains in critical medical care while handcuffed in hospital. Pike was sentenced to death for murdering Colleen Slemmer in 1995. Last Wednesday, she survived two failed lethal injections and was taken to hospital, where she stayed unconscious for days as staff cleared the injected chemical from her body.", "Experts and her legal team describe her apparent recovery as unprecedented. Deborah Denno, a criminologist at Fordham Law School, said she was \"absolutely astonished\" that Pike is conscious and speaking. While seven other prisoners have survived scheduled executions, in those cases executioners could not inject anything into their veins. Pike is believed to be the only person to survive a lethal injection, as she was actually injected with a toxin.", "Authorities have not said whether they will try again to execute Pike, nor have they explained what went wrong with the chemical pentobarbital. Tennessee Governor Bill Lee suspended all executions for the rest of the year, and the state's prisons chief said he plans to resign. Pike's attorneys are due in court in Nashville on Wednesday and will hold a news conference outside.", "Dr Joel Zivot, an anaesthesiologist advising Pike's defence team, said recovery from lethal injection is rare. He suggested that the pentobarbital may have spread under her skin instead of entering her bloodstream, which could explain her survival. However, he warned that many unknowns remain, including how much of the drug entered her system and what her recovery will look like. \"I would not, in any way, say at this point that all the big risks are behind her,\" he said."], "paragraphs_zh": ["据律师称，田纳西州50岁死囚克里斯塔·派克上周处决失败后幸存，目前意识清醒并能说话。她仍在医院接受重症监护，并被戴上手铐。派克因1995年谋杀科琳·斯莱默被判处死刑。上周三，她经历两次注射死刑失败后幸存，被送往医院，数天昏迷不醒，医护人员为她清除体内注射的化学物质。", "专家和她的法律团队称她的明显康复是前所未有的。福特汉姆法学院犯罪学家黛博拉·丹诺表示，她对派克能清醒说话感到“绝对震惊”。虽然另有七名囚犯在预定处决中幸存，但在那些案例中，行刑者未能将任何药物注入他们的静脉。据信派克是唯一在注射死刑中幸存的人，因为她确实被注射了毒物。", "当局尚未表示是否会再次尝试处决派克，也未解释戊巴比妥这种化学物质出了什么问题。田纳西州州长比尔·李暂停了今年剩余时间的所有处决，该州监狱负责人表示计划辞职。派克的律师定于周三在纳什维尔出庭，并将在法院外举行新闻发布会。", "派克辩护团队的麻醉师乔尔·齐沃特博士表示，从注射死刑中恢复的情况极为罕见。他提出，戊巴比妥可能扩散到她皮肤下，而非进入血液，这或许能解释她的幸存。然而，他警告仍有许多未知因素，包括有多少药物进入她体内，以及她的康复将如何。他说：“我现在绝不会说，所有重大风险都已过去。”"], "body": "Christa Pike, a 50-year-old death row inmate in Tennessee, is conscious and speaking after surviving a failed execution attempt last week, according to her lawyers. She remains in critical medical care while handcuffed in hospital. Pike was sentenced to death for murdering Colleen Slemmer in 1995. Last Wednesday, she survived two failed lethal injections and was taken to hospital, where she stayed unconscious for days as staff cleared the injected chemical from her body.\n\nExperts and her legal team describe her apparent recovery as unprecedented. Deborah Denno, a criminologist at Fordham Law School, said she was \"absolutely astonished\" that Pike is conscious and speaking. While seven other prisoners have survived scheduled executions, in those cases executioners could not inject anything into their veins. Pike is believed to be the only person to survive a lethal injection, as she was actually injected with a toxin.\n\nAuthorities have not said whether they will try again to execute Pike, nor have they explained what went wrong with the chemical pentobarbital. Tennessee Governor Bill Lee suspended all executions for the rest of the year, and the state's prisons chief said he plans to resign. Pike's attorneys are due in court in Nashville on Wednesday and will hold a news conference outside.\n\nDr Joel Zivot, an anaesthesiologist advising Pike's defence team, said recovery from lethal injection is rare. He suggested that the pentobarbital may have spread under her skin instead of entering her bloodstream, which could explain her survival. However, he warned that many unknowns remain, including how much of the drug entered her system and what her recovery will look like. \"I would not, in any way, say at this point that all the big risks are behind her,\" he said.", "body_zh": "据律师称，田纳西州50岁死囚克里斯塔·派克上周处决失败后幸存，目前意识清醒并能说话。她仍在医院接受重症监护，并被戴上手铐。派克因1995年谋杀科琳·斯莱默被判处死刑。上周三，她经历两次注射死刑失败后幸存，被送往医院，数天昏迷不醒，医护人员为她清除体内注射的化学物质。\n\n专家和她的法律团队称她的明显康复是前所未有的。福特汉姆法学院犯罪学家黛博拉·丹诺表示，她对派克能清醒说话感到“绝对震惊”。虽然另有七名囚犯在预定处决中幸存，但在那些案例中，行刑者未能将任何药物注入他们的静脉。据信派克是唯一在注射死刑中幸存的人，因为她确实被注射了毒物。\n\n当局尚未表示是否会再次尝试处决派克，也未解释戊巴比妥这种化学物质出了什么问题。田纳西州州长比尔·李暂停了今年剩余时间的所有处决，该州监狱负责人表示计划辞职。派克的律师定于周三在纳什维尔出庭，并将在法院外举行新闻发布会。\n\n派克辩护团队的麻醉师乔尔·齐沃特博士表示，从注射死刑中恢复的情况极为罕见。他提出，戊巴比妥可能扩散到她皮肤下，而非进入血液，这或许能解释她的幸存。然而，他警告仍有许多未知因素，包括有多少药物进入她体内，以及她的康复将如何。他说：“我现在绝不会说，所有重大风险都已过去。”", "text": "Christa Pike, a 50-year-old death row inmate in Tennessee, is conscious and speaking after surviving a failed execution attempt last week, according to her lawyers. She remains in critical medical care while handcuffed in hospital. Pike was sentenced to death for murdering Colleen Slemmer in 1995. Last Wednesday, she survived two failed lethal injections and was taken to hospital, where she stayed unconscious for days as staff cleared the injected chemical from her body. Experts and her legal team describe her apparent recovery as unprecedented. Deborah Denno, a criminologist at Fordham Law School, said she was \"absolutely astonished\" that Pike is conscious and speaking. While seven other prisoners have survived scheduled executions, in those cases executioners could not inject anything into their veins. Pike is believed to be the only person to survive a lethal injection, as she was actually injected with a toxin. Authorities have not said whether they will try again to execute Pike, nor have they explained what went wrong with the chemical pentobarbital. Tennessee Governor Bill Lee suspended all executions for the rest of the year, and the state's prisons chief said he plans to resign. Pike's attorneys are due in court in Nashville on Wednesday and will hold a news conference outside. Dr Joel Zivot, an anaesthesiologist advising Pike's defence team, said recovery from lethal injection is rare. He suggested that the pentobarbital may have spread under her skin instead of entering her bloodstream, which could explain her survival. However, he warned that many unknowns remain, including how much of the drug entered her system and what her recovery will look like. \"I would not, in any way, say at this point that all the big risks are behind her,\" he said.", "vocab": [{"word": "death row", "pos": "noun", "zh": "死囚牢房", "note": "指等待处决的囚犯区域"}, {"word": "inmate", "pos": "noun", "zh": "囚犯", "note": "常用于监狱语境"}, {"word": "execution", "pos": "noun", "zh": "处决", "note": "法律上的死刑执行"}, {"word": "lethal injection", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "注射死刑", "note": "一种处决方式"}, {"word": "conscious", "pos": "adj", "zh": "有意识的", "note": "反义词为unconscious"}, {"word": "unprecedented", "pos": "adj", "zh": "前所未有的", "note": "形容从未发生过的事"}, {"word": "astonished", "pos": "adj", "zh": "震惊的", "note": "表示极度惊讶"}, {"word": "criminologist", "pos": "noun", "zh": "犯罪学家", "note": "研究犯罪问题的专家"}, {"word": "suspend", "pos": "verb", "zh": "暂停", "note": "常指正式停止某事一段时间"}, {"word": "resign", "pos": "verb", "zh": "辞职", "note": "主动放弃职位"}, {"word": "anaesthesiologist", "pos": "noun", "zh": "麻醉师", "note": "负责麻醉的医生"}, {"word": "bloodstream", "pos": "noun", "zh": "血流", "note": "血液在体内的循环系统"}], "title_original": "US death row inmate Christa Pike awake and speaking after failed execution, lawyers say", "summary_original": "Experts and lawyers called the apparent recovery unprecedented, noting she is believed to be the only known person to survive a lethal injection.", "body_original": "US death row inmate Christa Pike awake and speaking after failed execution, lawyers say\nBy\nSareen Habeshian\nand\nKwasi Gyamfi Asiedu\nPublished\n6 October 2026\nUpdated 57 minutes ago\nUS death row inmate Christa Pike is \"conscious and speaking\" after surviving a failed execution attempt last week, her lawyers say.\nPike, 50, continues to receive critical medical care while handcuffed in hospital, her attorneys said in a statement on Tuesday.\nPike, who was sentenced to death after murdering Colleen Slemmer in 1995, survived two failed lethal injections last Wednesday in Tennessee. She was taken to hospital, where she remained unconscious for days as medical staff cleared her body of the injected chemical.\nExperts and her legal team say her apparent recovery is unprecedented. She is believed to be the only person to survive a lethal injection.\nHer lawyers called her progress \"medically unprecedented\", and while her prognosis remains unclear, \"at a minimum, we expect a long recovery\".\nDeborah Denno, a criminologist and professor at Fordham Law School, said she was \"absolutely astonished\" that Pike is conscious and speaking.\nThere were seven other cases where prisoners survived slated executions, but in those cases, executioners were not able to inject anything into the inmates' veins, Denno told the BBC.\nPike \"is the only person for whom some kind of toxin has been injected,\" she said.\n\"They did everything they were supposed to do as part of the execution process, and it simply didn't work,\" Denno said. \"This has never happened before.\"\nAuthorities have not yet said whether they will try again to execute Pike. They have also not offered an explanation for what went wrong after injecting her with the chemical pentobarbital.\nTennessee Governor Bill Lee suspended all executions for the rest of the year - and the head of prisons in the state said over the weekend that he plans to resign.\nPike was 18 when she and her then-boyfriend, Tadaryl Shipp, beat, tortured and killed 19-year-old Slemmer, whom they had met at a job training camp for troubled teens.\nPike's attorneys are scheduled to appear in court in Nashville on Wednesday. They also plan to hold a news conference outside the court.\nDr Joel Zivot, an anaesthesiologist advising Pike's defence team, said on Tuesday that the likelihood of recovering from lethal injection is low.\n\"Most people who get lethal injection die from it,\" he told the BBC. \"In fact, pretty well everyone, except Christa. So, the fact that she survived it ... was unusual.\"\nBut there remains a lot of uncertainty and many unknowns, he said, including how much of the pentobarbital got into her system, what her blood levels were after the injection and what her recovery will look like.\n\"I would not, in any way, say at this point that all the big risks are behind her,\" he noted.\nZivot had previously said the two doses of pentobarbital she received last week would have been enough that, had it entered her bloodstream in normal circulation, \"she would have surely died\".\nInstead, Zivot said a possible explanation is that instead of entering Pike's bloodstream, the pentobarbital was more likely to have spread across the tissue under her skin.\nZivot said last week he thought her ending up with a brain injury was \"very possible\", due to the delays in resuscitating her. He also believed it would take about a week to truly understand her condition and do a neurological exam. It's now been six days since the failed attempt to execute her.\nPike's lawyers previously warned that her medical history and anatomy - including thrombocytosis (a blood-clotting condition) and small veins - meant there was a risk she would experience \"unnecessary\" pain and suffering during a lethal injection.\nThey said on Tuesday that she has endured \"severe damage\" to her arms.\nRelated topics\nTennessee\nCapital punishment\nUnited States\nMore on this story\nI interviewed Christa Pike 20 years ago - I can't stop thinking about her\nPublished\n3 days ago\nTennessee prison chief to resign after Christa Pike's failed execution\nPublished\n3 days ago\nWhat happened in the failed execution of Christa Pike - and what next?\nPublished\nJust now", "fetched_at": "2026-10-07T00:57:05.204052", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Christa", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.488, "sm": 100, "em": 487, "cs": 0, "ce": 7, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "Pike", "s": 0.5, "e": 0.838, "sm": 500, "em": 837, "cs": 8, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": ",", "s": 0.838, "e": 1.025, "sm": 837, "em": 1025, "cs": 12, "ce": 13, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "a", "s": 1.025, "e": 1.087, "sm": 1025, "em": 1087, "cs": 14, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "50", "s": 1.1, "e": 1.232, "sm": 1100, "em": 123